cord here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them, more than any other pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 47% of normal for November to December and 56% for October to November. So far in 2026 the middle sits at 49% for March to April and 61% for February to March. Grid 19995 had its driest year in 1988 at 63%.</p>"}
